{"ts": 1784365546.3903575, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire episode. The trade ran from 0 to a peak of about +90pts by t=12m, confirming the entry thesis was correct, then gave back most of the gain in a steady grind down to roughly +4 to +11pts by t=23m without ever crossing into negative territory. That erosion looked like profit-giveback on a winning trade, not a wrong-direction entry -- the price never actually went against the entry, so there was no clean wrong-direction signal to bail on. Next time I would watch the rate and persistence of decay off a peak more closely (t12-t19 lost about 70pts steadily) as an early trim or protect-profit signal even though it does not meet the bar for a wrong-direction bail.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 24}
